                        "sense_id": "f68a10c0-0328-3e82-bd96-c85ec08f32d2",
                        "entry_id": "8e2d595e-6197-344b-8e1d-e040f3f1cdae",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Conspirationnisme teinté de spiritualité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "neologism"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ec8d067c-6556-4770-a6bd-65780069421e",
                                "sense_id": "f68a10c0-0328-3e82-bd96-c85ec08f32d2",
                                "text": "Les cercles francophones montrent aussi des accointances avec le monde de la conspiritualité. Des personnalités comme le conférencier en développement personnel Jean-Jacques Crèvecoeur, bien connu de la sphère antivaccin depuis la pandémie, revendiquent leur pratique du yoga."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b74e132-8bb8-4c95-90dc-a00d36cd4888",
                                "sense_id": "f68a10c0-0328-3e82-bd96-c85ec08f32d2",
                                "text": "En Australie, et comme dans de nombreux pays, l’intérêt pour les théories du complot et leur propagation a fortement augmenté pendant la pandémie de Covid-19. Le terme de conspiritualité qui décrit la fusion des théories du complot et la spiritualité, notamment New Age, semble s’appliquer à ces théories fleurissantes."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "60132eab-45e3-4632-a57c-65aa057882fd",
                        "source_entry_id": "8e2d595e-6197-344b-8e1d-e040f3f1cdae",
                        "source_sense_id": "f68a10c0-0328-3e82-bd96-c85ec08f32d2",
                        "target_lang_word": "conspirituality",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "conspirituality",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "82c491a5-23c2-3959-95b7-ba2eabbda0ef",
                                        "entry_id": "15d83ac5-23c7-375c-8b80-865462bcbd2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A political and spiritual ideology that combines alternative or New Age beliefs with conspiracy theories."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6e0edc8-956f-4179-8195-8bc2b382b9c0",
                                                "sense_id": "82c491a5-23c2-3959-95b7-ba2eabbda0ef",
                                                "text": "A hybrid of conspiracy theory and alternative spirituality has appeared on the internet. The existence of such a synthesis has previously been noted in passing (Barkun; Goodrick-Clarke), but no detailed account has yet been given of what, for the sake of convenience, we call ‘conspirituality’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11ed2192-44b6-4d0b-84ab-9992cfb9c916",
                                                "sense_id": "82c491a5-23c2-3959-95b7-ba2eabbda0ef",
                                                "text": "“Conspirituality” prompts us to focus on the cross-sections of conspiracy culture and alternative spirituality, and to the internal tensions there"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6c872fdd-e437-43e7-9998-ff6dfb273c85",
                                                "sense_id": "82c491a5-23c2-3959-95b7-ba2eabbda0ef",
                                                "text": "Conspirituality, in fact, helps describe some of the dynamics and one of the “contexts” in which Italian Pagan conspiracy-believing is embedded—one that, at a more general level, is characterized by what Christopher Partridge (e.g., 2004; 2005; 2014) defined as occulture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
